  "title": "Monochromatic reachability in arc-colored digraphs",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Conjecture For every $k$, there exists an integer $f(k)$ such that if $D$ is a digraph whose arcs are colored with $k$ colors, then $D$ has a $S$ set which is the union of $f(k)$ stables sets so that every vertex has a monochromatic path to some vertex in $S$.",
